\description{
\strong{Synthetic data.} This dataset contains no real participant responses. It
is drawn from the estimated parameters of the published three-class latent
profile solution in Liang and Ark's Study 2, so that the analysis can be
taught reproducibly. The authors' original data are not redistributed here.

Five bystander-action indicators define three profiles: a \emph{supportive-only}
profile (high emotional support, low everything else), a \emph{disengaged}
profile (uniformly low), and a \emph{broad responder} profile (uniformly high).
}
\section{Interpretation warning}{

